WEBVTT

00:49.466 --> 00:51.134
These biscuits are good.

00:55.180 --> 00:59.017
Say… Will you tell me what my suit is?

01:07.317 --> 01:08.651
That guy you're paired with…

01:10.236 --> 01:12.238
He's a murderer, you know?

01:13.907 --> 01:14.866
What?

01:14.949 --> 01:16.493
I saw him in the papers.

01:17.535 --> 01:18.620
He's Sunato Banda,

01:19.788 --> 01:23.208
an infamous killer
who took the lives of four women.

01:23.958 --> 01:26.628
I think he was sentenced to death.

01:27.670 --> 01:29.631
That's a lie.

01:29.714 --> 01:30.757
It's the truth.

01:31.674 --> 01:35.220
I think he's the Jack of Hearts.

01:38.556 --> 01:39.766
There are five of us left.

01:40.683 --> 01:44.437
I'm sure that the Jack will go
on the offensive now.

01:46.564 --> 01:47.649
Let's tell each other's suits.

01:53.029 --> 01:56.074
You're in a good position now.

01:57.408 --> 01:59.285
The Jack trusts you.

02:00.161 --> 02:03.706
You're the only one
who can lie to the Jack.

02:05.166 --> 02:08.837
In other words,
the only person who can end this game

02:09.671 --> 02:11.005
is you.

02:16.970 --> 02:19.472
It seems you still can't trust me.

02:20.598 --> 02:26.062
In any case, to make sure
that Banda is telling you the truth,

02:27.021 --> 02:29.607
I think you and I should
tell each other's suits.

02:31.818 --> 02:34.821
Do you really think I can trust you?

02:35.780 --> 02:37.407
It doesn't matter to me if you can't.

02:38.408 --> 02:40.827
The more choices you have, the better.
Isn't that right?

02:42.412 --> 02:44.080
I swear to you, I'll tell the truth.

02:45.582 --> 02:48.001
It's also true that Banda is a murderer.

02:51.087 --> 02:52.463
I can't trust you.

02:53.464 --> 02:58.303
Well, I'm sure we'll see
who's right this round.

03:00.471 --> 03:01.931
Your suit is spade.

03:06.269 --> 03:07.645
Tell me what mine is.

03:12.442 --> 03:13.359
Hey.

03:14.110 --> 03:15.612
I told you yours.

03:17.947 --> 03:19.282
I didn't agree to this deal.

03:26.998 --> 03:27.999
Heart.

03:42.472 --> 03:43.473
What's wrong?

03:52.023 --> 03:53.274
The Jack of Hearts…

03:55.235 --> 03:56.069
is that guy.

04:00.198 --> 04:01.991
I also suspected him.

04:04.077 --> 04:05.161
But don't worry.

04:07.163 --> 04:10.124
He'll die this round.

04:22.011 --> 04:23.721
That Banda guy…

04:26.140 --> 04:28.935
We need to be extremely cautious of him.

04:32.355 --> 04:35.525
The young guy who first lied
to that big guy and killed him…

04:36.651 --> 04:40.363
It was this guy
who told the young guy to lie.

04:43.825 --> 04:44.659
I saw him do it.

04:46.744 --> 04:48.413
He looks kind.

04:48.496 --> 04:52.250
But in reality,
he completely lacks empathy for others.

04:53.001 --> 04:56.421
He only has a theoretical understanding
of other people's feelings.

04:59.424 --> 05:01.676
He's the kind
who kills people for pleasure.

05:05.179 --> 05:07.223
I think he's the Jack.

07:06.050 --> 07:10.471
There are only five people left,
and I've lost my partner.

07:13.724 --> 07:18.229
A minute ago,
that Matsushita guy told me my suit.

07:19.397 --> 07:23.568
But I don't think he trusts me,
so I think he probably lied.

07:25.236 --> 07:29.365
You know, you look really honest.

07:29.449 --> 07:31.617
I don't think you'd lie.

07:32.827 --> 07:36.664
Could you please tell me what my suit is?

07:38.541 --> 07:41.502
Of course, I'll tell you
what your suit is.

07:42.128 --> 07:43.129
And I'll be truthful.

07:48.342 --> 07:52.597
You sure seem to be
infatuated with that Yaba guy.

07:53.639 --> 07:55.600
That's how a con man works, you know.

08:11.449 --> 08:12.783
I won't beat around the bush.

08:14.076 --> 08:15.536
Are you the Jack of Hearts?

08:18.039 --> 08:19.373
The only way

08:20.750 --> 08:22.293
I can answer that question

08:23.169 --> 08:25.588
is to say it could be either you or me.

08:30.885 --> 08:34.096
Just as I thought,
I doubt you and I can get along.

08:36.432 --> 08:37.558
Your suit…

08:38.935 --> 08:39.894
is heart.

08:41.729 --> 08:42.855
Mine…

08:44.649 --> 08:45.566
is club, right?

08:57.245 --> 08:58.454
These ones are better.

09:46.586 --> 09:47.587
Five people left.

09:48.337 --> 09:49.589
There are two pairs.

09:50.464 --> 09:52.758
The Jack will surely move this round.

10:03.603 --> 10:04.812
Well…

10:05.521 --> 10:07.398
This must be the final round.

10:25.666 --> 10:26.584
Heart.

10:33.841 --> 10:34.925
Thank you.

10:47.271 --> 10:48.189
Diamond.

10:59.867 --> 11:00.868
Spade.

11:12.421 --> 11:14.215
Okay, tell me mine now.

11:19.595 --> 11:20.429
Spade.

11:24.058 --> 11:26.143
It is time to make your guess.

11:26.727 --> 11:30.856
Everyone, please enter a prison cell.
One person per cell, please.

11:38.614 --> 11:41.951
ROUND 13

11:44.161 --> 11:47.790
The suit Matsushita told me
is most certainly a lie.

11:49.083 --> 11:52.211
And Kotoko ignored my question.

11:53.712 --> 11:54.797
This means

11:55.756 --> 11:58.342
I'm either diamond or spade.

12:02.430 --> 12:04.306
Ultimately, I'll have to go

12:05.724 --> 12:06.809
with intuition.

12:25.161 --> 12:27.246
Please make your guess.

13:15.044 --> 13:16.504
I won.

13:37.816 --> 13:40.402
You're the Jack of Hearts,
just as I thought.

13:43.906 --> 13:44.740
How…

13:44.823 --> 13:48.577
I saw when you and the murderer,
Banda, paired up.

13:50.579 --> 13:51.872
Let's be friends.

13:55.459 --> 13:56.502
Even if

13:57.086 --> 13:59.588
you were impressed by what Banda said,

14:00.172 --> 14:04.677
there's no way anyone could be
accepting of a stranger so quickly.

14:07.972 --> 14:11.392
There aren't many people
who'd approach someone like me.

14:14.603 --> 14:16.522
And if you tried to kill me,

14:17.106 --> 14:18.857
then you're either scheming,

14:18.941 --> 14:22.528
you're just a plain idiot,
a psychopath, or a sociopath.

14:23.821 --> 14:24.697
Why you…

14:25.573 --> 14:28.158
To find that out, I decided to play along.

14:29.869 --> 14:32.538
You thought that you could control me.

14:33.622 --> 14:38.335
Also, you were confident
that you were superior to everyone else.

14:39.670 --> 14:45.968
And the more important your position is,
the more your confidence manifests itself.

14:47.344 --> 14:49.221
Like the Jack of Hearts.

14:49.305 --> 14:51.181
Sorry, but it's not me.

14:51.265 --> 14:53.100
Banda is the Jack.

14:53.809 --> 14:54.768
It's such a shame,

14:59.607 --> 15:00.524
but it's not him.

15:11.577 --> 15:13.412
You were in cahoots with Kotoko.

15:14.622 --> 15:16.874
I told Kotoko her real suit.

15:18.584 --> 15:19.752
But still, she died.

15:22.755 --> 15:23.756
This means

15:24.840 --> 15:28.510
somebody else was controlling Kotoko.

15:30.387 --> 15:31.430
Then…

15:32.806 --> 15:34.642
Then that guy must be him.

15:34.725 --> 15:36.477
When I was in the cafeteria,

15:37.436 --> 15:41.523
each of you would always come
and get snacks around the same time.

15:44.360 --> 15:46.195
What do you think?

15:47.196 --> 15:48.280
Who should go first?

15:56.455 --> 15:57.331
Every time,

15:58.666 --> 16:00.376
you'd get the same type of snacks.

16:08.676 --> 16:11.887
You and Kotoko used
the cafeteria to communicate.

16:12.846 --> 16:13.847
Spade…

16:15.391 --> 16:19.687
Both of you pretended
that you were being controlled.

16:28.445 --> 16:30.447
Those snacks come in four flavors.

16:32.449 --> 16:35.369
You used the snacks that you got…

16:36.120 --> 16:39.999
to confirm with each other
whether your suit was right or not.

16:56.598 --> 16:57.933
Then…

16:58.726 --> 17:01.270
you told Kotoko
to lie to me about my suit.

17:02.479 --> 17:03.439
Diamond.

17:06.525 --> 17:09.028
I honestly did trust that woman.

17:11.488 --> 17:12.573
Except at the end.

17:15.617 --> 17:17.870
When did you three start working together?

17:18.454 --> 17:20.539
In the opening announcement for this game,

17:21.040 --> 17:24.126
they said that it's a test
of how much you can trust others.

17:25.335 --> 17:27.337
We simply followed that advice.

17:29.882 --> 17:32.468
The surest way to ensure trust

17:33.302 --> 17:36.555
isn't through persuasion, manipulation,
or even domination,

17:37.389 --> 17:39.850
nor is it through brainwashing, hypnotism,

17:40.601 --> 17:42.603
deception, or fear.

17:45.939 --> 17:47.024
It's equality.

17:54.615 --> 17:58.035
Just as I thought,
I doubt you and I can get along.

17:58.744 --> 17:59.620
By the way,

18:01.622 --> 18:06.668
why are you participating
in the games in this land?

18:10.589 --> 18:12.091
Until now,

18:12.841 --> 18:15.594
I've never been in a land
as beautiful as this one.

18:19.556 --> 18:20.933
Because I believe

18:21.975 --> 18:26.230
this is the only world
that is worthy of my control.

18:29.483 --> 18:32.653
I think you and I might be very similar.

18:37.116 --> 18:39.118
I thought the same thing.

18:40.828 --> 18:43.122
Trust is important in this game.

18:46.500 --> 18:52.297
I think I've finally found
an equal partner worthy of my trust.

18:58.762 --> 18:59.763
Still…

19:00.389 --> 19:03.892
It's still possible that
one of you is the Jack of Hearts!

19:04.518 --> 19:08.272
Yeah, maybe I did try to deceive you guys,

19:08.772 --> 19:12.693
but you can't declare
I'm the Jack of Hearts just based on that!

19:13.485 --> 19:14.945
I wouldn't be so sure.

19:15.028 --> 19:15.863
What?

19:16.488 --> 19:19.908
If those two were certain

19:20.492 --> 19:22.703
that you were the Jack of Hearts,

19:23.579 --> 19:28.917
then why didn't Banda lie to you
during the last round and try to kill you?

19:35.048 --> 19:36.633
They must have made a deal

19:38.218 --> 19:41.180
and are going to try
to get some info out of you.

19:56.028 --> 19:58.280
Round 14 will now start.

20:02.659 --> 20:03.744
What are you going to do to me?

20:05.913 --> 20:10.042
One doesn't often get the chance to have
a nice long conversation with a citizen.

20:10.626 --> 20:12.878
You'll tell us everything
you know about this land.

20:18.091 --> 20:20.427
It's unfortunate that I can't kill you.

20:24.681 --> 20:26.600
But I can still have fun with you.

20:38.862 --> 20:42.449
TEIO PRISON

21:20.487 --> 21:22.322
We couldn't get that much out of him.

21:23.615 --> 21:26.785
I guess he couldn't handle it
and guessed wrong on purpose.

21:27.828 --> 21:30.664
And we even told him
the truth about his suit.

21:32.457 --> 21:34.418
He gave up sooner than I expected.

21:49.683 --> 21:51.351
I am Kaito Kameyama.

21:52.060 --> 21:53.854
- It was…
- I'm going outside Tokyo.

21:55.063 --> 21:56.606
It's fun here.

21:57.441 --> 21:58.775
Since there are no laws,

21:58.859 --> 22:01.403
you can steal or kill
without being punished.

22:02.279 --> 22:03.697
When I'm playing a game,

22:04.197 --> 22:07.200
it's like nothing matters at all!

22:08.702 --> 22:09.953
It feels pretty damn good.

22:11.872 --> 22:13.707
I fucking hate this place.

22:13.790 --> 22:16.460
That's why I smoke weed…

22:18.045 --> 22:19.713
and cower.

22:23.300 --> 22:25.010
What is this world?

22:26.595 --> 22:28.096
What are these games?

22:28.680 --> 22:30.891
Who the heck is organizing them?

22:33.060 --> 22:34.186
Are you alright?

22:35.771 --> 22:38.690
Don't just film us! Give me a hand!

22:40.233 --> 22:41.568
You must be insane!

22:52.204 --> 22:54.539
Here, life is meaningless.

22:58.543 --> 23:00.170
Human life has no value.

23:02.506 --> 23:05.092
Is that what this world
is trying to teach us?

23:30.033 --> 23:31.076
Arisu…

23:31.660 --> 23:32.536
Do it!

23:32.619 --> 23:33.745
You couldn't return, right?

23:33.829 --> 23:35.288
We'll all die!

23:54.182 --> 23:55.058
There.

23:55.642 --> 23:56.768
Thank you.

24:02.941 --> 24:03.942
When…

24:07.404 --> 24:09.823
I heard Kyuma's last words,

24:12.033 --> 24:13.285
I realized something.

24:16.163 --> 24:18.165
They had originally been players.

24:19.875 --> 24:20.959
But now,

24:22.294 --> 24:24.504
they'd become citizens
and were making games here.

24:29.217 --> 24:30.177
It means…

24:32.596 --> 24:36.683
even if we clear all these games,

24:39.186 --> 24:41.438
we might not be able to go back.

24:45.233 --> 24:46.318
The world

24:48.612 --> 24:51.031
that we came from may not exist anymore.

24:54.492 --> 24:55.577
Did I…

24:57.871 --> 24:59.706
kill Tatta…

25:01.124 --> 25:02.334
just for that?

25:17.390 --> 25:18.600
That can't be true.

25:20.810 --> 25:22.979
I'm sure we can go back.

25:24.564 --> 25:25.649
I'm going for it.

25:27.275 --> 25:28.485
I'll keep playing the games.

25:31.863 --> 25:33.156
For Tatta's sake too.

25:46.836 --> 25:48.046
Are you really leaving?

25:48.755 --> 25:53.385
I'm still worried about Ann and Chishiya.
I'm going to look for them.

25:55.804 --> 25:59.391
We'll need more teammates if
we're going to defeat the King of Spades.

26:00.392 --> 26:04.688
If we can clear even one game,
we'll be closer to our goal.

26:07.899 --> 26:09.067
Don't you worry.

26:09.567 --> 26:11.403
I swear, we'll meet again someday.

26:13.405 --> 26:16.825
Usagi, you need to take a little break.

26:19.619 --> 26:20.620
Arisu!

26:21.121 --> 26:22.539
You take care of Usagi.

26:26.501 --> 26:28.586
Okay, take care of yourselves.

27:20.555 --> 27:22.015
Oh, well.

27:22.515 --> 27:24.976
Wish I could go to some unknown place.

27:28.521 --> 27:31.232
It would be bad if zombies
were to appear in Shibuya, huh?

27:31.316 --> 27:33.860
If they're all bitten here,
they will all turn into zombies!

27:33.943 --> 27:36.363
Stop it with the zombie talk,
and think about which shop to go to.

27:36.446 --> 27:39.449
But if zombies were to appear,
I guess only Karube would survive.

27:39.532 --> 27:41.201
You'd knock those zombies out
with one punch.

27:42.118 --> 27:43.411
No, it wouldn't be me.

27:43.495 --> 27:44.954
You'd be the one to survive, Arisu.

27:45.497 --> 27:46.956
Me? Why?

27:48.291 --> 27:49.959
I'm sure you're the one who will survive.

28:02.389 --> 28:03.223
What's your deal?

28:04.599 --> 28:06.726
You think your life's over now?

28:07.936 --> 28:08.978
What?

28:10.146 --> 28:12.565
Quit making that face
like it's the end of the world.

28:13.817 --> 28:15.819
I wasn't sure what you wanted to tell us,

28:17.028 --> 28:18.446
but it was pretty stupid.

28:20.490 --> 28:23.618
Is your life so pathetic that missing
some dumb interview will end it?

28:24.411 --> 28:26.579
Who cares about that stupid shit?

28:26.663 --> 28:28.081
Your dad pulled some strings?

28:28.164 --> 28:30.667
Just blow it off
and figure out what to do later.

28:31.835 --> 28:32.669
Arisu.

28:33.503 --> 28:36.923
In life, even when it seems like
you've hit a dead end,

28:37.006 --> 28:40.760
you turn a corner, and there'll be
a narrow road leading you further.

28:46.266 --> 28:49.894
That's not very convincing
coming from a part-time bartender.

28:50.478 --> 28:53.022
Then you say something cool.
You have any good ideas?

28:53.106 --> 28:54.858
Well, let me see…

28:55.442 --> 28:56.484
What? You don't?

28:57.777 --> 28:59.404
- But what you said was cool.
- Oh, fuck off.

29:00.530 --> 29:02.031
My mind went totally blank.

29:02.115 --> 29:03.199
Enough of your shit, man.

29:46.367 --> 29:47.202
It's mugwort.

30:16.189 --> 30:17.899
Say, why don't we go hunting?

30:19.692 --> 30:22.070
We're out of food, you know?

30:23.655 --> 30:24.948
If we don't get anything,

30:25.990 --> 30:27.283
it'll be weeds for dinner again.

30:38.294 --> 30:39.212
Here!

30:41.089 --> 30:43.842
If you want meat, then give me a hand.

31:05.905 --> 31:06.739
Arisu!

31:29.762 --> 31:31.389
Get to it, would you, Arisu?

31:34.851 --> 31:36.519
There's no food for dinner.

31:45.653 --> 31:46.988
Arisu! There! Over there!

32:00.126 --> 32:01.294
Over there!

32:11.721 --> 32:12.764
I see it.

32:22.565 --> 32:24.150
You almost had it!

32:24.233 --> 32:26.319
What's your problem?

32:29.572 --> 32:30.782
Darn it!

32:36.245 --> 32:37.455
Over there!

32:37.538 --> 32:38.665
Oh! Over here!

32:39.374 --> 32:40.458
Usagi, over there!

32:45.505 --> 32:46.339
Oh, darn!

32:47.006 --> 32:48.091
Arisu, over there!

32:56.349 --> 32:58.142
Oh, I can't get it.

32:59.310 --> 33:00.895
It's just no good.

33:01.479 --> 33:03.106
No dinner tonight.

33:04.524 --> 33:05.942
But I'm starving.

35:03.601 --> 35:04.602
Are you okay?

35:09.524 --> 35:10.858
The film…

35:12.568 --> 35:13.528
Film?

35:33.172 --> 35:34.006
It's in here.

35:58.948 --> 36:00.283
He must have been a photographer.

36:06.831 --> 36:08.249
This is 8mm film.

36:11.294 --> 36:12.461
Do you watch it with this?

36:54.337 --> 36:55.713
I am Kaito Kameyama.

36:56.881 --> 36:59.383
In this world
where electronics don't work,

37:00.384 --> 37:02.136
I want to use this 8mm film camera

37:02.637 --> 37:05.097
to make a record of this world
in order to discover

37:07.183 --> 37:08.809
the truth and reality of it.

37:12.939 --> 37:14.440
It's fun here.

37:14.941 --> 37:16.400
Since there are no laws,

37:16.901 --> 37:18.861
you can steal or kill
without being punished.

37:19.445 --> 37:21.113
When I'm playing a game,

37:21.197 --> 37:24.408
it's like nothing matters at all!

37:25.576 --> 37:27.078
It feels pretty damn good.

37:29.080 --> 37:30.498
I fucking hate this place.

37:31.082 --> 37:33.584
That's why I smoke weed

37:34.835 --> 37:36.462
and cower.

37:42.677 --> 37:45.388
It has been 26 days
since everyone disappeared.

37:57.066 --> 37:58.442
What are you doing?

38:00.820 --> 38:01.654
That's Ann.

38:10.079 --> 38:11.831
Excuse me. What's wrong?

38:15.501 --> 38:18.671
The fish are increasing in numbers
and the vegetation is becoming denser.

38:19.714 --> 38:21.299
The farther from the city center,

38:22.008 --> 38:24.010
the more the city is
covered in vegetation.

38:24.719 --> 38:26.679
Isn't it because there are no more humans?

38:27.179 --> 38:28.889
Of course, that's part of it.

38:29.473 --> 38:32.143
But the vegetation is growing
at an incredible pace.

38:33.644 --> 38:36.397
Each person came to this world
at different times,

38:36.981 --> 38:41.235
and food rotted quickly,
so time isn't flowing normally.

38:45.448 --> 38:46.365
Where are you going?

38:49.285 --> 38:50.953
I'm going outside of Tokyo.

38:52.121 --> 38:54.290
I want to know just what this world is.

39:01.255 --> 39:04.091
It has been 33 days
since everyone disappeared.

39:05.092 --> 39:07.094
I learned something from a man I met.

39:08.471 --> 39:11.015
A community has been established
on the outskirts of Setagaya.

39:11.098 --> 39:12.600
I'm headed there now.

39:29.158 --> 39:32.161
I came to this community
because I heard there's someone here

39:32.244 --> 39:33.662
who remembers something strange.

39:34.497 --> 39:36.457
Can you take me to them?

39:37.208 --> 39:38.209
This way.

39:43.047 --> 39:44.965
What is it they remember?

39:46.300 --> 39:48.969
Do you remember
when you came to this world?

39:49.762 --> 39:51.514
Yeah, a little bit.

39:52.848 --> 39:56.352
So, did you see those fireworks then?

39:57.103 --> 39:58.020
Fireworks?

40:00.314 --> 40:03.067
Yes, I did. I saw them. I remember.

40:05.277 --> 40:06.779
I saw them too.

40:08.781 --> 40:10.574
This way. Come on.

40:23.003 --> 40:25.172
This lady's story is super realistic.

40:25.756 --> 40:26.674
Come on.

40:27.299 --> 40:28.801
Here. She's over here.

40:31.595 --> 40:34.348
Tell him that story about those fireworks.

40:36.600 --> 40:37.435
Yes.

40:38.436 --> 40:39.270
Oh…

40:40.479 --> 40:41.564
About the fireworks?

40:46.444 --> 40:49.697
You want to hear about the fireworks too?

40:50.739 --> 40:51.574
Yes.

40:54.702 --> 40:56.954
I guess nobody remembers it.

40:58.330 --> 40:59.373
What?

41:02.543 --> 41:04.044
When I was a child,

41:05.504 --> 41:08.757
I had holes drilled into my skull

41:08.841 --> 41:11.677
when I had an operation done on my brain.

41:13.846 --> 41:15.181
That might be why…

41:18.476 --> 41:23.314
But I seem to be the only one
who remembers everything about that day.

41:26.317 --> 41:31.405
When the fireworks appeared in the sky…

41:34.366 --> 41:39.497
They looked like fireworks in the sky.

41:41.499 --> 41:42.333
But

41:43.626 --> 41:45.878
actually, that wasn't…

41:47.838 --> 41:48.839
fireworks--

41:48.923 --> 41:50.257
He's here again!

41:55.387 --> 41:57.389
The King of Spades is here again!

42:31.590 --> 42:32.841
This film

42:35.135 --> 42:37.555
is the only proof that I lived.

42:40.474 --> 42:42.476
I must leave this film for others.

43:15.301 --> 43:16.302
Something is coming.

43:31.609 --> 43:32.610
This way, Arisu!

43:37.072 --> 43:38.157
Watch out!

43:38.699 --> 43:39.533
Go!

44:01.221 --> 44:02.056
Usagi!

44:14.026 --> 44:14.943
Hey!

45:27.724 --> 45:28.600
Usagi?

45:33.230 --> 45:34.106
Who's there?

46:01.675 --> 46:03.260
Are you a citizen?

46:04.678 --> 46:05.596
What?

46:07.556 --> 46:08.724
I guess you aren't.

46:11.643 --> 46:12.644
Ow…

46:13.896 --> 46:15.314
Then why did you attack me?

46:16.815 --> 46:18.984
If you had kept running,
you would have died.

46:21.195 --> 46:23.822
I told him to leave you
since you'd only be a drag,

46:25.157 --> 46:28.160
but he carried you
all the way here anyhow.

46:29.912 --> 46:30.913
"He"?

46:38.754 --> 46:41.256
You'd better go thank him, Arisu.

46:42.883 --> 46:44.051
How come you know my name?

46:44.760 --> 46:46.595
He told me.

46:52.768 --> 46:53.602
But be careful.

46:54.436 --> 46:56.563
Since you interfered with our plan,

46:56.647 --> 46:58.065
he's in a bad mood.

47:43.485 --> 47:44.319
Aguni…

47:47.281 --> 47:49.366
Yo, newbie.

50:26.732 --> 50:31.737
Subtitle translation by: Brian Athey
